{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Prepares for Final Exams"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Worst Course Ever"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le10ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking for Permission "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you ask for permission, it is important to be polite."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use a modal like <span class=\"italic\">can</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to ask for permission.<br/><br/>You can also ask a Yes or No question like \u201c<span class=\"italic\">Is it OK if \u2026 </span>\u201d or \u201c<span class=\"italic\">Would you mind if \u2026 </span>\u201d <br/><br/> Here are some ways to ask for and give permission."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asking for Permission\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Giving Permission\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can I see that? </span><br/> <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Would you mind if I changed courses?</span><br/> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can I take that course next term?</span><br/> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could I use your textbook this evening?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Of course!</span><br/> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">That's not a problem.</span><br/> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sure.</span><br/> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">OK, no problem.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Comparatives and Superlatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a comparative to compare somebody or something to <span class=\"strong\">one</span> other person or thing.<br/>  You use <span class=\"strong\">than</span> after comparatives.<br/>   You use a superlative to compare somebody or something to the whole <span class=\"strong\">group</span> that he, she or it belongs to.<br/> You add <span class=\"strong\">the</span> in front of the superlative form.<br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for information on how to form the comparative and superlative:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Comparative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"faster (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the fastest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Most adjectives:<br/>+er, +-est\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"late\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"later (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the latest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives ending in -e:<br/>+r, +-st\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happier (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the happiest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2-syllable adjectives ending in -y:<br/>+ier, +iest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"useful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more useful (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the most useful<br/>the least useful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2+-syllable adjectives:<br/><br/>more - less + adjective+ than<br/><br/>the most - least + adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good<br/>bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"better (than)<br/>worse (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best<br/>the worst\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular comparisons\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "financial records"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the list of expenses and revenues of a business"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Introduction to Accounting is about how to keep financial records. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about business courses."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reputation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way people think about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Digital Reputation Management is a good course."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "digital "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes something that is practical and helpful"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think the most useful course is Effective Negotiation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "public relations"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "everything related to how customers communicate with a company"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Public Relations is a very broad topic."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "effective"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes something that works well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The course is about ways companies can be more effective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "customer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who buys a product or service"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Public Relations includes everything related to customer experience. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of the names of 6 crazy courses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 3 courses that are good."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write sentences comparing the good courses. Use the words <span class=\"italic\">good</span>, <span class=\"italic\">better</span>, <span class=\"italic\">best</span>. Explain why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 3 courses that are bad. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write sentences comparing the bad courses. Use the words <span class=\"italic\">bad</span>, <span class=\"italic\">worse</span>, <span class=\"italic\">worst</span>. Explain why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I invent 6 crazy courses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare the good courses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare the bad courses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my sentences to a partner."}]}], "labs"